WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.567 --> 00:00:02.567
-Good evening, I'm Seth Meyers,
and this is "Late Night."

00:00:02.567 --> 00:00:04.000
We hope you're doing well
tonight.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:05.467
And now if you don't mind,
we're going to get to the news.

00:00:05.467 --> 00:00:08.934
The White House announced on
Friday that President Biden had

00:00:08.934 --> 00:00:11.767
a cancerous skin lesion removed
from his chest.

00:00:11.767 --> 00:00:14.767
And the lesion is already
running two points ahead

00:00:14.767 --> 00:00:16.067
of DeSantis.

00:00:16.067 --> 00:00:18.467
[ Laughter ]

00:00:18.467 --> 00:00:21.567
Former president Trump
attended CPAC over the weekend

00:00:21.567 --> 00:00:25.834
and told reporters he would not
drop out of the 2024 election

00:00:25.834 --> 00:00:27.601
if he's indicted on criminal
charges.

00:00:27.601 --> 00:00:30.734
You know, we compare him
to a mobster all the time,

00:00:30.734 --> 00:00:33.567
but now he's literally saying,
"No problem,

00:00:33.567 --> 00:00:35.901
I can still run things
from the joint."

00:00:35.901 --> 00:00:38.400
[ Laughter ]

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:40.267
In his speech over
the weekend at CPAC,

00:00:40.267 --> 00:00:42.767
former president Trump
said that before he came along,

00:00:42.767 --> 00:00:45.567
the Republican Party was run
by freaks and fools.

00:00:45.567 --> 00:00:51.000
Yeah. Nothing like the
Rhodes scholars we have today.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:53.167
That's like going to Orlando
and saying, "You know,

00:00:53.167 --> 00:00:55.267
it wasn't always this nice."

00:00:55.267 --> 00:00:58.067
[ Laughter ]

00:00:58.067 --> 00:01:01.100
Donald Trump Jr.'s
fiancee Kimberly Guilfoyle spoke

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:04.200
over the weekend at CPAC, and
it looked like a rousing speech

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:06.400
until they cut to the audience.
Take a look.

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:10.501
&gt;&gt; All of us in this room have
one message to Joe Biden --

00:01:10.501 --> 00:01:14.634
it is time to put America first!

00:01:14.634 --> 00:01:17.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:17.601 --> 00:01:19.033
[ Laughter ]

00:01:19.033 --> 00:01:22.267
Which brings us to a segment
called "Where is Everybody?!"

00:01:22.267 --> 00:01:25.200
♪♪

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:27.901
Where is everybody?
I've never seen a theater

00:01:27.901 --> 00:01:31.801
that empty, and I used to do
long-form improv.

00:01:31.801 --> 00:01:33.200
[ Laughter ]

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:35.334
I've been in elevators more
crowded than that.

00:01:35.334 --> 00:01:36.934
Where is there --

00:01:36.934 --> 00:01:40.400
Did they accidentally schedule
you against Kid Rock karaoke?

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:44.067
That speech must have taken
twice as long

00:01:44.067 --> 00:01:47.400
just to account for the echo.

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:48.801
Speaking of,
why are you yelling?

00:01:48.801 --> 00:01:51.000
It's not like you need to play
to the back of the house.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:53.767
And what's this,
"All of us in the room

00:01:53.767 --> 00:01:55.601
have one message for Joe Biden."

00:01:55.601 --> 00:01:58.434
You're the only one there.

00:01:58.434 --> 00:02:00.801
There couldn't be a second
message in the room

00:02:00.801 --> 00:02:02.367
for Joe Biden.

00:02:02.367 --> 00:02:04.267
If anything, that room
has one message for you --

00:02:04.267 --> 00:02:05.767
bring it way down.

00:02:05.767 --> 00:02:07.100
[ Laughter ]

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:10.267
-This has been
"Where is Everybody?!"

00:02:10.267 --> 00:02:11.801
It's a hit.
It's a hit new segment.

00:02:11.801 --> 00:02:14.100
[ Laughter ]

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:16.167
Florida governor Ron DeSantis
spoke yesterday

00:02:16.167 --> 00:02:17.968
at the Ronald Reagan
presidential library.

00:02:17.968 --> 00:02:20.968
Specifically, he said
"All these gotta go."

00:02:20.968 --> 00:02:23.968
[ Laughter ]

00:02:26.133 --> 00:02:28.300
TV host Rachael Ray has
announced she's ending

00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:30.133
her talk show after 17 seasons.

00:02:30.133 --> 00:02:32.467
She made the decision in less
than 30 minutes,

00:02:32.467 --> 00:02:34.367
but at home,
it would take you two hours.

00:02:34.367 --> 00:02:37.334
[ Laughter ]

00:02:38.567 --> 00:02:39.801
Didn't do great.

00:02:39.801 --> 00:02:41.667
Better than I thought
I would do.

00:02:41.667 --> 00:02:45.634
So that's kind --
I'm not saying it's a win/win.

00:02:45.634 --> 00:02:49.033
It was definitely a win/lose,
but...

00:02:49.033 --> 00:02:51.200
A woman in Florida recently set
a Guinness World Record

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:53.868
by winning 23 ultra-marathons
in 23 days.

00:02:53.868 --> 00:02:57.300
In less happy news, her car
is basically undrivable now.

00:02:57.300 --> 00:03:00.167
[ Laughter ]

00:03:00.167 --> 00:03:02.868
Finally, United Airlines has
announced it will offer

00:03:02.868 --> 00:03:05.467
T-Mobile customers free Wi-Fi
on all flights,

00:03:05.467 --> 00:03:08.601
and Spirit announced that
they're gonna fly really close,

00:03:08.601 --> 00:03:10.634
and you should be able to hop on
their network.

00:03:10.634 --> 00:03:11.901
[ Laughter ]

00:03:11.901 --> 00:03:13.334
[ Laughs ]

00:03:13.334 --> 00:03:16.133
Good Photoshop.
Good Photoshop.

00:03:16.133 --> 00:03:18.300
That was the monologue,
everybody.

